# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES/ADR-053 §2 D5 — THE MODEL'S ONE-WAY DOOR ON A VAULTED BLOCK IS DROPPED
# `Samen.Scopes.Docs.BlockVault` is the model-level refusal that keeps a `DocBlock` in the vault:
# any update that would clear `text_secure` (or give a vaulted block a plain `text` twin) is
# refused at the governed write path. This patch makes the stored classification read as `:plain`
# whatever the row actually holds, so both predicates go quiet: a clear SUCCEEDS, the row leaves
# the vault, its ciphertext is gone and the operator plane stops masking it.
#
# Aimed at the guard ONLY. `Samen.Web.Notes.Writes` still classifies writes from the row (its own
# `keep_classification/2`), so the ordinary editor path stays green — this is the layer BELOW the
# helper, proven at the model. The "defence in depth" c10 test also stays green on purpose: it
# pins the OTHER mechanism (Ash drops a `text_secure: nil` change it cannot attribute to a
# `%Ash.NotLoaded{}` column), which this patch does not touch.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/docs_scope_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a declassifying update (plain text in, text_secure nulled) is REFUSED
# MUST_FAIL: even a bare `text_secure: nil` (no plain text at all) is refused
# MUST_FAIL: a vaulted block cannot gain a plaintext twin
# MUST_FAIL: a changeset with NO original data cannot clear the vault
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/docs/block_vault.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/docs/block_vault.ex
@@ -106,10 +106,7 @@
   # write is not (see `writes_plain_twin?/2`).
   defp stored_classification(changeset) do
     case Ash.Changeset.fetch_data(changeset, :text_secure) do
-      {:ok, nil} -> :plain
-      {:ok, %Ash.NotLoaded{}} -> :unknown
-      {:ok, _vaulted_value} -> :vaulted
-      :error -> :unknown
+      _ -> :plain
     end
   end
 end
